1. Open Mozilla Firefox browser.
2. Launch Selenium IDE extension.
3. Select **Create New Project** from the welcome window.
4. Enter the project name as **Login Test** and click OK.
5. Click on the **Record** button.
6. Enter the base URL: `https://www.selenium.dev/` and click **Start Recording**.
7. The browser will automatically open the Selenium website.
8. Right-click on the website and select **Selenium IDE**.
9. Click **Assert** and select **Title**.
10. Return to Selenium IDE and review the recorded steps such as open, click, etc.
11. Add a new test case named **TC2** and click Add.
12. Open the Selenium website and navigate to the **Getting Started** section.
13. Review the three main options: Selenium WebDriver, Selenium IDE, and Selenium Grid.
14. Open the Selenium IDE page from the Selenium website.
15. Use the website navigation to access the available Selenium resources.
16. Use the browser context menu on the Help page when required.
17. Right click on "Need Help > Assert > Text"
18. Return to Selenium IDE and review the recorded steps.
19. Verify the recorded commands such as **open, click, and assert**.
